 "title": "Comparative Genomics and Gene Annotation Tools",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around gene annotation and comparative genomics tools. UniProt and UniProtKB are central entities, with UniProt having algorithms from AlphaFold and DeepMind, and UniProtKB having annotations from these algorithms and a database from UniProt. OrthoDB is used by OrthoLoger and uses KEGG, while BRAKER2 has higher accuracy than BRAKER1 and a higher F1 score than TSEBRA. EVM has a lower F1 score than BRAKER2. GenBank hosts NCBI, and SGD is an authority for both GenBank and UniProtKB. Bioinformatics research has been published by Oxford University Press, and OrthoDB has been funded by the Swiss National Science Foundation.",
